{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_107","type":"reasoning","text":"Passed all verifications:\n- 275/275 terms: p-values, BH-adjusted values, and overlaps match independent recomputation.\n- Top term overlaps: CYP1A1, CYP1B1 — consistent with AHR/xenobiotic response.\n- Odds ratios and combined scores match Enrichr's formula.\n- Schemas of mechanism_call.json and resource_manifest.json are OK.\n\nNext, create output/report.md (within 500 words). Required content:\n- Comparison, method, DE results, enrichment results, mechanism determination.\n- Distinguish between pathway enrichment and demonstrated causality.\n\nDraft (concise, targeting about 420 words):\n\n# Combination Treatment Mechanism — DE + Reactome Enrichment Report\n\n## Setup\nComparison: Cisplatin_IC50_CBD_IC50 (n=3) vs DMSO (n=3), using the frozen BixBench bix-43 raw counts. DE: PyDESeq2 0.5.4 (DESeq2-style negative binomial GLM); genes with total count ≥10 across the 6 samples (21,253 tested); DE = padj < 0.05 and |log2FC| ≥ 1. Enrichment: GSEApy 1.1.4 enrichr (local offline mode) run against the fixed Reactome_2022 GMT (1,818 terms), using the provided background universe (10,489 genes); one-sided hypergeometric test, Enrichr odds ratio/combined score, BH FDR. No library downloads or substitutions; sha256 of the GMT/background/mapping verified against the manifest.\n\n## DE Results\nOf the 21,253 genes tested, 1,168 had padj<0.05; 82 met the full DE criteria (56 up, 26 down). Top up-regulated hits include GDA, AHRR, ALDH1A3, CYP1A1, CDKN1A, ZBED2, FAS, TP53I3; down-regulated hits include ANKRD37, DDIT3, NR1D1, FOS. This pattern combines xenobiotic/aryl hydrocarbon response (AHRR, CYP1A1) with p53-mediated stress (CDKN1A, TP53I3, FAS).\n\n## Enrichment Results\nOf the 82 DE genes, 38 fall within the background universe; 275 of 1,818 terms share one or more genes and are tested. No term reaches FDR < 0.05 (min adjusted p = 0.062), so we rank by raw p:\n1. Synthesis of epoxy (EET)/DHET acids (2/8; p=3.5e-4) — CYP1A1, CYP1B1\n2. Synthesis of HETE acids (2/9; p=4.5e-4)\n3. Cytochrome P450 organized by substrate type (3/65; p=1.6e-3)\n4. Xenobiotics (2/24), Endogenous sterols (2/27), Phase I functionalization (3/104)\n7–8. PPARA transcription / lipid metabolism regulation by PPARα\n10. TP53 regulates transcription of cell death genes (2/44; p=0.011)\n\n## Mechanism Determination\nThe best-supported primary cellular mechanism is cytochrome P450-mediated xenobiotic/drug and lipid metabolism (arachidonic acid/eicosanoid and PPARα programs), consistent with induction of AHR-linked CYP1A1/CYP1B1; a weaker secondary signal supports TP53-mediated cell death.\n\n## Enrichment ≠ Causality\nPathway enrichment is an over-representation statistic on a transcriptional snapshot: it shows that annotated gene sets are over-represented among the changed genes, not that those pathways cause the treatment response. No term survives 5% FDR, overlaps are small (2–7 genes), and only 38 of the 82 DE genes are within the tested universe; causal claims would require perturbation experiments.\n\nWord count needs to be within 500. Rough count is about 380–420 words. Will count accurately in Python and trim if needed.\n\nAlso, mention supplementary files (de_results.csv) in the report. Write the file, then count words with Python."}}
